Track 2: Chrysalis Junkyard of Doctor Nawa
- Story & Context: Hidden in the storage wing where decommissioned particle injectors rust beneath sea-salt mist, Mariko penned this raw confession about her arranged marriage collapse while Doctor Nawa—the facility's half-mad former chief physicist—poured shochu over the tape heads to keep them cool. The track strips the Southern boogie down to a weeping acoustic bottleneck slide and a frantic, single-djembe heartbeat, capturing the scent of solder and bruised papaya as Mariko whispers into a crystal microphone: "I smashed the shell with both my hands, so don't you dare come looking for the girl I used to be."
