Track 3: Phase-Lock Swarm Crossing the Strait
- Story & Context: Myth holds that during the island-wide electrical blackout of August 1978, the band hot-wired the club’s diesel generators directly into the accelerator's main transformer coils, creating an acoustic shockwave that literally steered migrating monarch butterflies down the beach and into the tunnel mouth. Thousands of clubgoers danced barefoot on wet gravel while the twin guitars traded blistering solos against four tuned djembes, Mariko leading an ecstatic, gospel-infused Japanese chorus shouting: "Ten thousand wings riding down the beam, nobody's touching the earth tonight!"
